    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(A)=P(A\\mid B)P(B)+P(A\\mid\\overline{B})P(\\overline{B})$.\n\nPartition $A$ into $A\\cap B$ and $A\\cap\\overline{B}$, then apply the conditional probability formula.",
      "worked": "The events $A\\cap B$ and $A\\cap\\overline{B}$ are disjoint and together make up $A$. Using the conditional probability formula,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=P(A\\cap B)+P(A\\cap\\overline{B})\\\\P(A)&=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}P(B)+\\frac{P(A\\cap\\overline{B})}{P(\\overline{B})}P(\\overline{B})\\\\P(A)&=P(A\\mid B)P(B)+P(A\\mid\\overline{B})P(\\overline{B}).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
